          <!-- 22. Conclusion -->
          <section id="s22" class="wp-section scroll-mt-24">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-ink mb-6">22. Conclusion</h2>
            <p>Xhavic does a specific set of things, and we think it does them well. Over 2,000 TPS at $0.04 per transaction with sub-200ms latency, settled on Ethereum. Modular architecture where each component can be upgraded independently. Full EVM bytecode compatibility so nothing breaks when you migrate.</p>
            <p>The Dual Wallet System is the headline feature. Two execution paths, separated at the protocol level, serving fundamentally different risk profiles within a single network. The Instant Wallet handles composable DeFi at speed. The Secured Wallet gives institutions the safety they need for high-value operations.</p>
            <p>Native oracle integration and AI-agent execution support are our bet on where on-chain activity is headed. Autonomous systems interacting directly with decentralized infrastructure, not through duct-taped middleware.</p>
            <p>The scaling path from 12,000 TPS today to 120,000+ through sharding is architecturally ready — Phase III delivers it. The challenges are real: DA costs, withdrawal latency, sequencer centralization during launch. We've been honest about every one of them.</p>
          </section>

